\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 +}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  CF:0020}}$
{\footnote \pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 $}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 Workings of the Clic report system}}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf2\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Workings of the Clic report system
\par }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par Clic 3.0 registers the users' activity repo
rts in a database. This database is normally called CLICDB.MBD, and is usually found in the same folder as Clic (in computers not on a network), or in a network folder to which all the stations have writing rights. To understand how the CLICDB.MDB base wo
rks internally, you are recommended to consult the section }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Structure of the database}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 ESTRUCTURA}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 .
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 In the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
Options - Global Options }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 of}{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
Clic you can indicate the location of the CLICDB.MDB file, and other options such as authorising the students to create new users and groups or allowing them to consult their own reports.
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 The process that Clic uses to register reports is the following:

\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab 
If the report system is activated when Clic starts up, it will run an auxiliary programme called CLICREP.EXE. T
he function of this programme is to act as an intermediary between Clic and the database. The CLICREP.EXE file must always be found in the same folder as CLIC.EXE, and users must never try to activate or close it directly: Clic will always take charge of 
activating it when it is considered necessary. The presence of the CLICREP programme is only noted by the appearance of an icon when you use the combination ALT+TAB to pass from one programme to another.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab The first operation that Clic carries out is to call ClicRep to show the users' identification screen. The users have two options: Choose the group to which they belong and their name, or clicking on the }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Cancel }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button. In this case the connection between Clic and the database is interrupted, and they work without anything being registered in the report system.\line 
There is also the possibility to let the users register directly from the identification screen, clicking on the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 New user }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button. This button can be deactivated from the }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Global options }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 menu of Clic, as well as with the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 New group }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button that appears when a new user decides to register.
\line There is only one case in which the identification screen will not appear: when Clic has been activated with the parameter }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 /USER:XXX}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 , where XXX is the user 
code that will be used to register the session reports (these codes can be consulted in the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Maintenance of users and groups }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
screen). With this technique a personalised shortcut icon can be created for each user. For more information about accessing Clic with parameters consult the Clic's help document.\line The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Reports - New user }{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 menu of Clic allows you to activate anew the users' identification screen.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Once the user has been identified, Clic creates a new entry in the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 sessions}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  table of the datab
ase. Each registry of this table contains information about the user code and the date and time when the session was started. The current session can be interrupted and a new one started through the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
Reports - Begin new session }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 menu of Clic.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Each time that Clic loads an activity pack (PAC or PCC files) a new register is created in the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 pacs}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 table of the database. This table contains information about the pack name and the session in which it was activated. If the user runs an independent activity that doesn\rquote t belong to any pack (ASS, PUZ, SOP, CRW and TXA files) then an entry in the 
}{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 pacs}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  table is created, which shows a hyphen in the pack name.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab When the user finishes an activity, Clic registers the results in the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 acts}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  table of th
e database. Each registry in this table contains the name of the activity, the code of the pack to which it belongs, the time taken (in seconds), the number of attempts made, the correct answers, global precision and a logic field which indicates whether 
the activity was completed or not.\line The only activities that are never registered in the database are those of exploration, the information screens and all those that have the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Include in user reports }{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 field unchecked in the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Activity options}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 .
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par When the system 
works on a network all these transactions are performed simultaneously in a single file (CLICDB.MDB) that contains the database. Each station blocks the base while the information is being written, and this can lead to a queue of pending operations, which
 
slows down movement from one activity to the next. The speed in finishing the transactions depends on diverse factors: the capacity and speed of the network, the speed of each of the stations in finishing its work, access time to the server's hard disc, e
t
c. The most critical moment can be when Clic is started up from different stations simultaneously. As in all group operations carried out on a single file, a slow machine can cause a queue that affects faster stations: There is only one 'desk' and everybo
dy must wait their turn until the user who is occupying the server finishes his /her business.
\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
\par }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc back.bmp\}}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 INDEX}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057    Back to contents
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\keepn\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \page }{\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain 
