\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par This section of the programme allows you to carry out different operations relating to new users, dropouts and keeping the users' and group data clean.
\par 
\par Both the groups and users have a unique id
entification code that the programme assigns automatically, and which cannot be changed. The user will never get to see this code, but the system administrator may use it to create personalised icons that access Clic with the parameter }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 /USER:###}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . For more information about accessing Clic with parameters see the Clic's help document.
\par 
\par All users must belong to a group.
\par 
\par All groups and users must have a name to distinguish them from the others. There may be two users with the same name but in different groups, never in the same one. The maximum length of a group or user name is 80 characters.
\par 
\par Both Clic and ClicDB always show the group and user lists in alphabetical order. If you wish to change this order you may write a numerical expression in front of the nam
es. For example, if in the database the groups are defined as "First", "Second", "Third", "Fourth", "Fifth", and "Sixth", then the alphabetical order will be as follows:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li425\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin425\itap0 {\fs16\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Fifth
\par First
\par Fourth
\par Second
\par Sixth
\par }\pard \ql \li426\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin426\itap0 {\fs16\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Third
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
