\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li425\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin425\itap0 {\fs16\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 01 - First
\par 02 - Second
\par 03 - Third
\par 04 - Fourth
\par 05 - Fifth
\par }\pard \ql \li426\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin426\itap0 {\fs16\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 06 - Sixth
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par In the database there is a group and a user called ".Not identified". These registries cannot be eliminated and are designed to be used
 when carrying out tests with the report system without affecting the data of the other registered users. There is a full stop in front of the name so that they will always appear at the head of the list.
\par 
\par The groups and users can be identified by name or,
 optionally, by an image (BMP o ICO files: GIF are not accepted here) that will be shown in the list that Clic presents when starting the sessions. The maximum dimensions of these images are 68x68 pixels: if a bigger image is used the image will appear tr
uncated. In the network configurations it is best that the images be stored in the server's shared folder.
\par 
\par The options available in the Maintenance of users and groups screen are as follows:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Properties}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \line 
Allows you to modify the name and image assigned to each of the users and groups. It also permits you to see the code assigned to each user.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Create a new user or group}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \line This button adds a new group to the base, or a new user within the selected group.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Clean data}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \line 
With this option you can eliminate the data of all the activities, packs and sessions from a determined period of time by the selected group or user. The programme will show a warning message and then a window where you can indicate the initial and final 
dates of the period to be cleaned.\line The cleaning of group data means that the data of all its users will be erased.\line You are recommended to }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 compact}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 COMPACT}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  the database after using any of its cleaning functions.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Delete}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \line This button will totally 
eliminate the selected group or user from the database. It will also eliminate all the sessions, packs and activities that this user or group has used.\line The elimination of a group means the disappearance of all its users.\line 
You are also recommended to }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 compact}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 COMPACT}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  the database after any elimination.
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
In network configurations you are recommended to perform all registrations, deregistrations and cleaning when there are no other stations using Clic. The elimination or cleaning of a user who is active at that m
oment will cause an error in the report system.
\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
