\par In this window all the sessions of the users in a determined group are grouped according to their dates.
\par 
\par The drop-down list that appears in the upper left of the screen allows you to choose the name of the group that the report will refer to.
\par 
\par Initially there will be a global report that includes all the activities of every pack that has been used at any time by each and every member of the group. The list }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Data relative to...}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 allows you to limit the range of data to a determined pack. In the }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Reports by activity and pack}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 INFPAC}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 window you can obtain more detailed information about the results of a group with regard to a particular pack.
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 The button }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 From... to...}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  leads to a window in which you can indicate the period of time contemplated in the report.
\par 
\par The principal table shows the resumes of each of the dates on which the group used the selected pack: the number of activities done, ac
tivities completed, total time and global precision. Global precision is the average obtained by all the users of the group, and the other columns (including time) show the totals accumulated by each user.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Global summary }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 table shows the total and the average precision of all the sessions that appear in the main table.
\par 
\par The graph represents the evolution of two variables over a time: the global precision (the average precision of each user) and the percentage of solved activities in respect of the total number of activities done on each date.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Print}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 button allows you to carry out two different functions: to overturn the printer that appears in the image on the screen (including the graphic) or a list of the data in text format.
\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
