\par }{\b\fs24\cf2\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Reports on packs and activities
\par }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par In this window you can observe the results obtained by the users in a particular acti
vity pack or in a particular activity of a pack. The two lists in the upper left of the screen allow you to choose the pack or activity that the calculations will refer to.
\par 
\par The report can refer to all users, all users in a particular group, or just one user.
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 From... To...}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  button leads you to a window where you can indicate the period of time contemplated in the report.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Sessions}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  list shows, grouped by dates, all the times that a user has done the selected pack or activity. Clicking on the elements
 of the list will show a resume of the results obtained on that session: Activities done, activities solved, total time (the total time taken by all users) and the global precision average.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Global data}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  table indicates the number of users who have used
 the pack or activity, the number of sessions in which it has appeared, the number of activities done, activities completed, total time and the global precision average.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Pack evolution}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  graph represents two variables over a time: the global precision (
the average precision obtained on each date) and the percentage of activities solved in respect of the total number done.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Distribution of results}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  groups the results obtained in the activity or pack grouped by five columns: the left column represents t
he number of times that very low results have been obtained (between 0% and 20%), and the right column shows the highest results (from 80% to 100%).
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 User classification}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  is ordered from the global precision average obtained by everyone who has done the activity or pack. It is important to check the "}{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Acts" }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
column, where the number of times that each user has done the pack activities is shown, as someone who has only done an activity once but obtained a good result will be ahead of someone who has done th
e pack various times but with some errors. For more detailed information about a particular user's behaviour with a pack it is recommended to consult the user reports window.
\par 
\par The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Print}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  button allows you to carry out two different functions: to print the i
mage that appears in the screen (including the graphic) or a list of the data in text format. If you opt for the list, there is two further options available: print only the results of the selected session or print the r\'e9sum\'e9s of all the sessions.

\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
